# El Wataniya ERP - cron schedule example (Linux production)
# Copy into /etc/cron.d/elwataniya-backup and adjust paths.
# The job runs regardless of whether the application is running.
#
# Daily backup at 02:00 (change minute/hour as needed):
# 0 2 * * * root /opt/elwataniya/scripts/backup/backup.sh >> /var/log/elwataniya-backup.log 2>&1
#
# Daily restore-verification at 03:00 (proves backups can be restored):
# 0 3 * * * root /opt/elwataniya/scripts/backup/restore-verify.sh >> /var/log/elwataniya-restore-verify.log 2>&1
#
# Notes:
#  - Create scripts/backup/backup.env from backup.env.example with the correct
#    BACKUP_DIR, BACKUP_RETENTION_DAYS and BACKUP_EXTERNAL_COMMAND (off-server).
#  - Set POSTGRES_PASSWORD in the environment or backup.env for non-container pg_dump.
#  - The scripts fail loudly (non-zero exit) and are safe to run while the app is up.
